# Reveal fence grammars

## Root cause

Reveal's highlight plugin knows only its bundled languages. The Carve runtime plugin and generated static pages register no Carve, CSV, or TSV grammar, so their fences cannot receive separator tokens.

## Change

Depend on the published carve-grammars package and register its Carve, CSV, and TSV highlight.js definitions before Reveal runs its highlight plugin. Use the same registration in runtime and static pages, and test a rendered slide through the real highlighter.

## Scope

Registration is per highlight.js instance and applies to every slide in that deck. It does not inspect particular fence content or slide structure.
